# Sybaritic - A Spartan protocol library for Python

Now that Rogallo{a} supports multiple protocols{b}, it's tempting to add one or two more. As of the time of writing, alongside Gemini{c}, both Gopher{d} and Finger{e} are supported. While wandering the small web{f}, I stumbled on the Spartan protocol{g}. Given its similarity to Gemini and the fact it uses Gemtext{h} as its main document type, adding it to Rogallo seemed like an obvious thing to do.

=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/ {a} Rogallo
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/protocols/ {b} multiple protocols
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/gemini/ {c} Gemini
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/gopher/ {d} Gopher
=> https://rogallo.davep.dev/finger/ {e} Finger
=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/smolweb/ {f} small web
=> https://github.com/michael-lazar/spartan {g} the Spartan protocol
=> https://blog.davep.org/tag/gemtext/ {h} Gemtext

In aid of this, I've created Sybaritic{a}. It is, in effect, a sibling library to Wasat{b}, Port70{c} and Port79{d}. As with the others, it is async-all-the-way and is designed to have a similar API.

=> https://sybaritic.davep.dev/ {a} Sybaritic
=> https://wasat.davep.dev/ {b} Wasat
=> https://port70.davep.dev/ {c} Port70
=> https://port79.davep.dev/ {d} Port79

With this in place, I can now extend Rogallo to handle `spartan://` URIs as first-class citizens.

